# Secrets. There is exactly ONE file in this tree that holds the Anthropic API
# key, and it is this one: .env (KEY="sk-ant-..."), read by `make run` and
# handed to the guest at boot over QEMU's fw_cfg channel. Nothing the build
# produces can contain it, because the build is never told what it is.
#
# It used to be everywhere. `-DFABLEOS_API_KEY='"$(KEY)"'` put the live key
# inside net.o, kernel.elf, kernel.bin, fableos.iso and the .build-flags stamp
# (which recorded `KEY=sk-ant-...` in plain text), and this file was what kept
# those five artifacts out of git. That is the wrong place for a safety
# property: one `git add -f`, one CI cache, one shared build directory and the
# key is published. The Makefile has no KEY variable any more and passes no -D,
# so `grep -r sk-ant` over every build output finds nothing — the entries below
# are hygiene, not a containment measure.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Build artifacts
*.o
kernel.elf
kernel.bin
# The stamp that forces a full rebuild when EXTRA_CFLAGS changes. It used to
# record `KEY=sk-ant-...` verbatim; there is no KEY to record now.
.build-flags

# Dependency files from the compiler's -MMD -MP, one per object
*.d

# Host test binaries from `make test-host`. Leading **/ because a pattern with a
# slash in it is anchored to this file's directory, and the tree is tests/.
**/tests/build/

# Packet capture from `make run-pcap`
net.pcap

# The persistent disk (`make disk`, attached by `make run`). It is the machine's
# own storage: whatever the model wrote last time is in there, it can be
# hundreds of MiB, and it is not source. Never committed — but note the reason
# is size and churn, NOT secrecy: nothing secret is ever put in the image (the
# API key travels over fw_cfg into RAM and is never written to disk).
disk.img
*.img

# Bootable media from `make iso` (a 4 MB ISO and its staging tree)
fableos.iso
build/

# Scratch idea notes
ideas/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Appliance (Python)
appliance/.venv/
appliance/visual_check.png
__pycache__/
*.pyc
